{"content":[{"c":["ELIAB"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. Helon’s son and leader of Zebulun’s tribe when the Israelites were roaming in the Sinai wilderness after their escape from Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Num.1.9","r":"Num.1.9","rawR":"Num.1.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.1.9","value":"Num.1.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 1:9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.2.7","r":"Num.2.7","rawR":"Num.2.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.2.7","value":"Num.2.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:7"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.16","r":"Num.10.16","rawR":"Num.10.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.16","value":"Num.10.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:16"},"). As leader, he presented his tribe’s offering at the consecration of the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=Num.7.24,29","r":"Num.7.24,29","rawR":"Num.7.24,29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.7.24,29","value":"Num.7.24,29"}],"t":"ref","v":"7:24, 29"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. Member of Reuben’s tribe and son of Pallu. Eliab was the father of Nemuel, Dathan, and Abiram. Dathan and Abiram rebelled against Moses and Aaron in the wilderness (",{"href":"?bref=Num.16.1,12","r":"Num.16.1,12","rawR":"Num.16.1,12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.16.1,12","value":"Num.16.1,12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nm 16:1, 12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Num.26.8-9","r":"Num.26.8-9","rawR":"Num.26.8-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.26.8-9","value":"Num.26.8-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"26:8-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.11.6","r":"Deut.11.6","rawR":"Deut.11.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.11.6","value":"Deut.11.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 11:6"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["3. Jesse’s eldest son and brother of King David. An impressive person physically, he was rejected by God for the kingship in favor of David (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.16.6","r":"1Sam.16.6","rawR":"1Sam.16.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.16.6","value":"1Sam.16.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 16:6"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.2.13","r":"1Chr.2.13","rawR":"1Chr.2.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.2.13","value":"1Chr.2.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 2:13"},"). Eliab served King Saul when Goliath defied Saul’s army (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.17.13,28","r":"1Sam.17.13,28","rawR":"1Sam.17.13,28","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.17.13,28","value":"1Sam.17.13,28"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 17:13, 28"},"). He was appointed leader of Judah’s tribe during David’s reign (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.27.18","r":"1Chr.27.18","rawR":"1Chr.27.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.27.18","value":"1Chr.27.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 27:18"},"). His granddaughter Mahalath married King Rehoboam of Judah (",{"href":"?bref=2Chr.11.18","r":"2Chr.11.18","rawR":"2Chr.11.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Chr.11.18","value":"2Chr.11.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Chr 11:18"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["4. Variant name for Elihu in ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.6.27","r":"1Chr.6.27","rawR":"1Chr.6.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.6.27","value":"1Chr.6.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chronicles 6:27"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Elihu_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Elihu_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Elihu_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Elihu #1"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["5. Warrior from Gad’s tribe who joined David at Ziklag in his struggle against King Saul (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.9","r":"1Chr.12.9","rawR":"1Chr.12.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.9","value":"1Chr.12.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 12:9"},"). Eliab was an expert with the shield and spear (v ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.12.8","r":"1Chr.12.8","rawR":"1Chr.12.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.12.8","value":"1Chr.12.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"8"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["6. Levite musician assigned to play the harp in the procession when King David brought the ark to Jerusalem (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.15.18","r":"1Chr.15.18","rawR":"1Chr.15.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.15.18","value":"1Chr.15.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 15:18"},"). He was assigned permanently to service in the tabernacle (",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","r":"1Chr.16.5","rawR":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.16.5","value":"1Chr.16.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"16:5"},")."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Eliab","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Nm 1:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.1.9","rawQueryValue":"Num.1.9","sourceRefExact":"Num.1.9"},{"anchorText":"2:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.2.7","rawQueryValue":"Num.2.7","sourceRefExact":"Num.2.7"},{"anchorText":"10:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.16","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.16","sourceRefExact":"Num.10.16"},{"anchorText":"7:24, 29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.7.24,29","rawQueryValue":"Num.7.24,29","sourceRefExact":"Num.7.24,29"},{"anchorText":"Nm 16:1, 12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.16.1,12","rawQueryValue":"Num.16.1,12","sourceRefExact":"Num.16.1,12"},{"anchorText":"26:8-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.26.8-9","rawQueryValue":"Num.26.8-9","sourceRefExact":"Num.26.8-9"},{"anchorText":"Dt 11:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.11.6","rawQueryValue":"Deut.11.6","sourceRefExact":"Deut.11.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 16:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.16.6","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.16.6","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.16.6"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 2:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.2.13","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.2.13","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.2.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 17:13, 28","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.17.13,28","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.17.13,28","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.17.13,28"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 27:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.27.18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.27.18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.27.18"},{"anchorText":"2 Chr 11:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Chr.11.18","rawQueryValue":"2Chr.11.18","sourceRefExact":"2Chr.11.18"},{"anchorText":"1 Chronicles 6:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.6.27","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.6.27","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.6.27"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 12:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.12.9","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.12.9","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.12.9"},{"anchorText":"8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.12.8","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.12.8","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.12.8"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 15:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.15.18","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.15.18","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.15.18"},{"anchorText":"16:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.16.5","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.16.5","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.16.5"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"14405c4779d8af5944f8dea946c9d749cb8899ba7c3da57306e113b9b4f2a271","sourceItemName":"Eliab","sourceItemOrder":83,"sourceMember":"Articles/E.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Eliab","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Eliab","title":"Eliab","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}